/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (    The District consists of many neighborhoods that range in history, culture, and modernization across the city. A rule of thumb when traveling the District is to remember that the numbered streets go from north to south, lettered streets go east to west and diagonal streets are stated. The District is divided up into four quadrants: Southwest, Southeast, Northwest, and Northeast.)
/E (    The District consists of many neighborhoods that range in history, culture, and modernization across the city. A rule of thumb when traveling the District is to remember that the numbered streets go from north to south, lettered streets go east to west and diagonal streets are stated. The District is divided up into four quadrants: Southwest, Southeast, Northwest, and Northeast.)
