/T (Where The George Washington University and the Foggy Bottom area are located is in the Northwest quadrant. Other major features of Northwest include Georgetown, Dupont Circle, the U Street corridor, and the Woodley Park and Adams Morgan neighborhoods. As the largest quadrant, all Metro lines serve various parts of the Northwest quadrant except notably Georgetown, which is primarily accessible via the Circulator or Metrobus.)
